   "RaceName": "State Representative Pos. 2",
   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/>State Representative (2021-present), Health Care &amp;\r\nWellness Committee Chair, Labor &amp; Workplace Standards Committee Member, Transportation Committee Member, Joint Select Committee on Health Care &amp; Behavioral Health Oversight Co-Chair.<br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/>Captain, West Pierce Fire &amp; Rescue. Former Vice President,\r\nWest Pierce Firefighters IAFF Local 1488. Former Armor\r\nCrewman for the Washington Army National Guard.<br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/>Master&rsquo;s of Public Administration from the University of\r\nWashington, Bachelor&rsquo;s of Science from Eastern Oregon\r\nUniversity, Fire Service Program at Bates Technical College.<br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/>Pierce County Central Labor Council Delegate, Pierce\r\nCollege EMS Advisory Board.<br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/>As a Pierce County Firefighter, I&rsquo;ve been on the frontlines\r\nof our public safety crises for over two decades. As State\r\nRepresentative, I&rsquo;ve worked hard to find solutions to keep\r\nour families safe and ensure everyone can thrive. We&rsquo;ve\r\nmade progress by investing in law enforcement, lowering\r\nprescription drug costs and funding education, but there&rsquo;s\r\nmore to do. I will work to lower costs, support small\r\nbusinesses, and improve public safety. Together, we can find\r\ncommon sense solutions to our toughest challenges. I&rsquo;m proudly endorsed by nurses\r\n(WSNA) and West-Pierce Firefighters. I'd be honored to have your vote.<br/><br/>",
